    "title": "Gobblers come up just short, still searching for first win | Broadway | dnronline.com",
    "text": "Broadway put up a valiant effort, but ultimately came up short in a 53-48 non-district loss to Monticello at home on Wednesday.\nAfter trailing by nine at the half, the Gobblers cut the deficit to one by the end of the third, but ultimately came up short down the stretch and remained winless to start the year.\nBroadway was led by Landon Lipscomb-Showalter and Andrew Garber with nine points apiece.\nRyan Norton and Jeremiah Griffin added eight points each for the Gobblers, while Lance Slater totaled six and Caiden Rhodes chipped in with four.\nBroadway (0-3) will return to its home floor on Friday against non-district opponent and unbeaten Central.",
